# BetConstruct is iframe-first

BetConstruct integration uses BetConstruct-hosted iFrames. Do not invent a parallel Nextpari sportsbook or casino client for this provider.

## Do not build

- a Nextpari BetConstruct event feed
- Nextpari BetConstruct odds/markets UI
- a Nextpari BetConstruct betslip
- Nextpari BetConstruct casino/game UI
- BetConstruct odds ingestion into `sportsStore`
- synchronization of BetConstruct markets into the native sportsbook UI
- routing BetConstruct bets through the native Nextpari odds engine (`sports_engine_place`, LSports quotes, native betslip)

Native LSports sportsbook remains separate and unchanged.

## BetConstruct owns inside the iframe

Sportsbook UI, prematch, live, markets, odds, betslip, bet acceptance/trading UI, and casino/game UI.

## Nextpari owns

- player authentication
- short-lived currency-bound AuthToken / launch session
- active wallet and currency
- player balance
- Wallet Ledger (all actual player-money changes)
- provider callback endpoints
- security restrictions
- deposits/withdrawals outside the provider iframe
- provider accounting/reconciliation

## Sportsbook flow

Nextpari frontend requests a launch session from Nextpari backend → receives a short-lived currency-bound AuthToken → opens the BetConstruct iframe with `integrationMode=1` and `AuthToken`. BetConstruct then calls Nextpari Operator API: `GetClientDetails`, `GetClientBalance`, `BetPlaced`, `BetResulted`, `Rollback`.

## Casino flow

Nextpari frontend requests a casino game launch → opens the provider-hosted game iframe. BetConstruct RGS calls Nextpari Single Wallet: `Authentication`, `GetBalance`, `Withdraw`, `Deposit`, `WithdrawAndDeposit`, `Rollback`.

## Enablement

Keep the integration fail-closed until real test credentials, domain, SharedKeys, OperatorId, and IP allowlist are supplied. Do not treat dummy env as production-ready. Do not move player money until Wallet Ledger adapters are explicitly wired in a later phase.
